<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Tristao sees 23.5 mln bag coffee crop-trade.</title>
<headline>Brazil Tristao sees 23.5 mln bag coffee crop-trade.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian trade house Tristao has estimated Brazil's 1997/98 coffee crop will reach 23.5 million 60-kg bags in its first forecast of the year, Brazilian traders said.</p>
<p>Tristao has also revised upwards its forecast of the 1996/97 crop to 27.5 million bags from a previous figure of 25.85 million bags, they said.</p>
<p>A breakdown of both estimates was not immediately available.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
